Yes — the line 10–40 JSON “DAG wrapper” format is valid for your generator (same structure as the example). It’ll work as long as:
	•	the templates exist (emr-batch-trigger-sensor, emr-serverless-execution-stream-sss, placing_s3_sensor_object)
	•	BUCKET_NAME is available via include-airflow-variables
	•	your resource_link_name exists in the serverless config mapping

What resource_link_name is used for
	•	It’s the lookup key your template uses to fetch the EMR Serverless config (app id, execution role/ARN, and any env-specific settings) via GetServerlessConf(...).

Below are 5 separate DAG JSONs (no commas between them, 2 blank lines between each). Copy/paste and save each block as its own file.

{
  "dag-imports": [""],
  "dag-param": {
    "start_dt": "datetime.datetime(2026,1,15)",
